# Plan - tb-convergence-sweep-records

**Feature:** `tb-convergence-sweep-records`
**Spec:** [`spec.md`](spec.md)
**Design:** [`design.md`](design.md)
**Interview:** [`interview.md`](interview.md)
**Created:** 2026-11-26

## Strategy

One slice and one PR (FEATURE scope). New module
`plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/sweep-records.js` holds claim
validation, record construction, scope collection, the regression predicate
and the reviewer guide. Small call sites in `execution.js` (validation call,
packet fields, `roundPolicy.revision`, one instruction sentence) and
`boundary-review.js` (`roundSchedule`). The #134 fix is in
`review-findings.js`. Tests: new `cli/test/sweep-records.test.js`; #134 cases
in `cli/test/round-policy.test.js`. Existing tests that send
`{findingId, claim}` gain `disposition`.

## Steps

- **P1.** `sweep-records.js`: `checkClaims` (AC1, AC2 field paths);
  `execution.js` calls it in place of the inline loop. **Advances:** R1, R2.
- **P2.** Record construction from retained `fixed` claims (`classId` from
  history, `round` from the round policy); `scopeSweepRecords` from earlier
  boundary-review inputs of the open scope; packet `sweepRecords` and
  `roundPolicy.revision`. **Advances:** R3.
- **P3.** `roundSchedule` collects the scope's records; `blocks` adds the
  swept-class regression. **Advances:** R4.
- **P4.** Guide text and the instruction sentence. **Advances:** R5.
- **P5.** `review-findings.js` prepass: re-reported IDs count as present;
  grouping by round-policy scope, round and revision. **Advances:** R6.
- **P6.** `PROTOCOL.md`, `commands/pr-review.md`, desktop restage
  (`npm --prefix apps/desktop run stage:protocol`). **Advances:** R7.

## Verification

Focused: `node --test` on the new and touched test files with
`GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null`. Broad local: the CLI suite without the
host-dependent files (idle-inhibitor, scratch-cleanup, metrics-repair) on the
Mac. Final: hosted CI after review convergence.
